{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794596962903,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d6507bb4001c2p0y9mgU0TtbT","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d6506621001Gp0LpQGZ9guKIs","type":"tool","id":"call_6dca474519204dff9b02a006","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"for f in specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/*.md; do echo \"########## $f\"; grep -nE \"^### P[012]|^[0-9]+\\. \\*\\*|Case:|Review verdict|^## Next Focus|Focus area\" \"$f\" | head -30; done"},"output":"########## specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-001.md\n22:### P0 Findings\n26:### P1 Findings\n28:1. **`make no changes to` reads a genuine no-edit request as a change request** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- The fix adds `(?! (?:to|in)\\b)` after the `make no changes` alternative. The lookahead cannot tell a scope limit inside a change request from the object of a no-edit request, so it deletes the whole phrase whenever it is followed by `to` or `in`. `isNoEditRequest('make no changes to the tests')` now returns `false` where `isNoEditRequest('make no changes')` returns `true`, and the prompt is then treated as a change request: `attachCommand('sk-doc', {action:'route',selectionKind:'single',targets:[{workflowMode:'sk-create-agent'}]}, 'make no changes to the tests')` returns `/create:agent`. Before this commit the same prompt returned `undefined`. The two new tests at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:73-74` pin only the change-request direction, so nothing in the suite fails for this regression.\n32:   Case: `make no changes to the tests` -> `isNoEditRequest` returns `false` and `attachCommand` with a single-mode `sk-create-agent` route returns `/create:agent`; the same prompt with the phrase left bare (`make no changes`) returns `true` and `undefined`. Run with `tsx` against the current source (probe under the lineage directory).\n53:### P2 Findings\n55:1. **The guard matches a literal single space, so line-break and punctuation variants keep the pass-three defect** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- The lookahead is `(?! (?:to|in)\\b)`, with a literal space and no allowance for a newline, tab, doubled space or punctuation between the phrase and its object. Those forms match `make no changes` and are read as no-edit requests, so the change request loses its command -- the exact class `AR3-P2-001` reported. Inputs run: `refactor the parser and make no changes\\nto its public api`, `... make no changes  to its public api` (two spaces), `... make no changes\\tto its public api`, `... make no changes: to its public api`, `... make no changes, to its public api` each return `true` from `isNoEditRequest` and `undefined` from `attachCommand`.\n59:   Case: `refactor the parser and make no changes\\nto its public api` returns `true` from `isNoEditRequest`, so `attachCommand` returns `undefined` for the single-mode route and the change request keeps no command.\n94:## Next Focus\n97:- Focus area: the doctor hook check fix `nodeFlagSkipsScript` in `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, checked once\n103:Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n########## specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n21:### P0 Findings\n25:### P1 Findings\n29:### P2 Findings\n31:1. **A long flag whose value is attached by shell quoting still reports `ok` for a command node refuses to run** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:232` -- The name split only handles `=`. `readWords` merges a quoted value into the same word, so `node --eval\"1\" <marker>` reaches the flag test as `--eval1`, which is not in `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN` and is then skipped as an unknown long flag; the marker becomes the script word and the check prints `ok claude`. Node itself refuses the same command with `bad option: --eval1` (exit 9), so the hook cannot run while the check reports it wired. The short form is caught (`node -e\"1\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), while the long form is not: `node --check\"1\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) although node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.\n35:   Case: fixture `.claude/settings.json` with `node --eval\"1\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` -> `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <fixture>` printed `ok claude` and exited 0, while `node --eval\"1\"` itself exits 9 with `bad option: --eval1`.\n70:## Next Focus\n73:- Focus area: the safety consequence of the no-edit P1 across the four gates, the two fixes' test evidence, and comment/naming quality on the changed lines\n77:- Recovery note: the `Review verdict` line stays CONDITIONAL while `NE3-P1-001` is active.\n79:Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n########## specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-003.md\n22:### P0 Findings\n26:### P1 Findings\n30:### P2 Findings\n71:## Next Focus\n74:- Focus area: synthesis\n80:Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"########## specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-001.md\n22:### P0 Findings\n26:### P1 Findings\n28:1. **`make no changes to` reads a genuine no-edit request as a change request** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- The fix adds `(?! (?:to|in)\\b)` after the `make no changes` alternative. The lookahead cannot tell a scope limit inside a change request from the object of a no-edit request, so it deletes the whole phrase whenever it is followed by `to` or `in`. `isNoEditRequest('make no changes to the tests')` now returns `false` where `isNoEditRequest('make no changes')` returns `true`, and the prompt is then treated as a change request: `attachCommand('sk-doc', {action:'route',selectionKind:'single',targets:[{workflowMode:'sk-create-agent'}]}, 'make no changes to the tests')` returns `/create:agent`. Before this commit the same prompt returned `undefined`. The two new tests at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:73-74` pin only the change-request direction, so nothing in the suite fails for this regression.\n32:   Case: `make no changes to the tests` -> `isNoEditRequest` returns `false` and `attachCommand` with a single-mode `sk-create-agent` route returns `/create:agent`; the same prompt with the phrase left bare (`make no changes`) returns `true` and `undefined`. Run with `tsx` against the current source (probe under the lineage directory).\n53:### P2 Findings\n55:1. **The guard matches a literal single space, so line-break and punctuation variants keep the pass-three defect** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- The lookahead is `(?! (?:to|in)\\b)`, with a literal space and no allowance for a newline, tab, doubled space or punctuation between the phrase and its object. Those forms match `make no changes` and are read as no-edit requests, so the change request loses its command -- the exact class `AR3-P2-001` reported. Inputs run: `refactor the parser and make no changes\\nto its public api`, `... make no changes  to its public api` (two spaces), `... make no changes\\tto its public api`, `... make no changes: to its public api`, `... make no changes, to its public api` each return `true` from `isNoEditRequest` and `undefined` from `attachCommand`.\n59:   Case: `refactor the parser and make no changes\\nto its public api` returns `true` from `isNoEditRequest`, so `attachCommand` returns `undefined` for the single-mode route and the change request keeps no command.\n94:## Next Focus\n97:- Focus area: the doctor hook check fix `nodeFlagSkipsScript` in `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, checked once\n103:Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n########## specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n21:### P0 Findings\n25:### P1 Findings\n29:### P2 Findings\n31:1. **A long flag whose value is attached by shell quoting still reports `ok` for a command node refuses to run** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:232` -- The name split only handles `=`. `readWords` merges a quoted value into the same word, so `node --eval\"1\" <marker>` reaches the flag test as `--eval1`, which is not in `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN` and is then skipped as an unknown long flag; the marker becomes the script word and the check prints `ok claude`. Node itself refuses the same command with `bad option: --eval1` (exit 9), so the hook cannot run while the check reports it wired. The short form is caught (`node -e\"1\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), while the long form is not: `node --check\"1\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) although node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.\n35:   Case: fixture `.claude/settings.json` with `node --eval\"1\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` -> `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <fixture>` printed `ok claude` and exited 0, while `node --eval\"1\"` itself exits 9 with `bad option: --eval1`.\n70:## Next Focus\n73:- Focus area: the safety consequence of the no-edit P1 across the four gates, the two fixes' test evidence, and comment/naming quality on the changed lines\n77:- Recovery note: the `Review verdict` line stays CONDITIONAL while `NE3-P1-001` is active.\n79:Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n########## specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-003.md\n22:### P0 Findings\n26:### P1 Findings\n30:### P2 Findings\n71:## Next Focus\n74:- Focus area: synthesis\n80:Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"for f in specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/*.md; do echo \\\"########## $f\\\"; grep -nE \\\"^### P[012]|^[0-9]+\\\\. \\\\*\\\\*|Case:|Review verdict|^## Next Focus|Focus area\\\" \\\"$f\\\" | head -30; done\"}"},"time":{"start":1794596961204,"end":1794596962903}}}}
