{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597012805,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d6513c8a001SPMxjYwVqT5kzi","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d650c64b001i3HBiwROVBajZ5","type":"tool","id":"call_d8a036a738814b398a6e98cd","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n -A40 \"SA2-P2-002\\|NO_EDIT_REQUEST misses\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/iterations/iteration-002.md | head -80"},"output":"66:- `spec_code` — partial. The `run` policy means \"safe to start without asking\" and the table honours it; the no-edit wording is narrower than the packet's stated intent, recorded as `SA2-P2-002`.\n67-- `checklist_evidence` — pending. No checklist claim in focus.\n68-- `feature_catalog_code` — pending; `command-meaning-matching.md` and the command-bridges README are the traceability iteration's job.\n69-- `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `playbook_capability` — pending / notApplicable.\n70-\n71-## Integration Evidence\n72-\n73-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:478-485` is the only production path that turns an attached command into a `policy`; it reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS` (`:483`), not `COMMAND_ROWS`, which is why the 11 row-less commands still carry a policy.\n74-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:20` imports `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` from the same module, so a widening of the pattern changes the scorer's read-only lift and the attach gate together — the single-vocabulary property the pass-one comment claims.\n75-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts:554-560` keeps the async backend probe on the command path only, so the synchronous recommend reader never performs a network call.\n76-\n77-## Edge Cases\n78-\n79-- **Pattern copied, not widened.** The current `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` is byte-identical to the base `fusion.ts:675` inline regex (`git show 35c3188681:…/fusion.ts`). Recorded so the vocabulary finding is read as pre-existing wording that the new gate now exposes, not as a regression the fix introduced.\n80:- **`start` vs `run`.** Every command the no-edit gap would attach is `start` or `ask`; the only `run` rows are read-only or add-only. That is what keeps `SA2-P2-002` at P2 instead of P1.\n81-- **Row-less commands.** Eleven tracked commands have no `COMMAND_ROWS` entry, so their `mutating` class is not recorded anywhere on the attach path. Read as out of reach for this iteration: those commands are all `start` or `ask`, so the missing class cannot turn into a `run` offer.\n82-\n83-## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n84-\n85-- `command-attach.ts:289` — pattern is a stateless, non-global regex, so repeated `.test()` calls cannot alternate.\n86-- `command-attach.ts:329` — the gate sits before any table lookup and returns `undefined`, so no command and no policy are produced.\n87-- `advisor-status.ts:224-231`, `:318-326` — database handles close on every path, including the error path; a failed close is reported as `unavailable`, not swallowed.\n88-- `advisor-status.ts:424-434` — the integrity probe is opt-in on the sync reader and default-on in `handleAdvisorStatus` (`:553`), and a transient lock/IO reason does not force a rebuild.\n89-- `derive-command-bridges.cjs:1121-1143` — a runnable with no policy record throws at generation time rather than defaulting to a permissive class.\n90-\n91-## Ruled Out\n92-\n93-- **A `run` row that mutates.** Ruled out by executed enumeration: 19 run rows, 0 `mutates`.\n94-- **The `COMMAND_POLICIES` deletion removing policy from row-less commands.** Ruled out: policy travels in `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, 0 mismatches against rows for the 52 commands that have both.\n95-- **`advisor_status` leaking holdout prompt text.** No prompt source is read on this surface; the residual is that the privacy test cannot prove it (`SA2-P2-003`).\n96-- **Path traversal through `skill_nodes.source_path` in `readIndexStaleness`.** Read as not a leak: the file is read only to hash it, the hash is compared with a hash from the same database, and no content or path is returned to the caller. A writer of that row already controls the artifact.\n97-\n98-## Next Focus\n99-\n100-- Dimension: traceability\n101-- Focus area: the changed docs in this area — `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` and `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` — against the code they describe (`fusion.ts` command-meaning gate, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`), plus the pass-one `R4-P2-001` prose claim that `COMMAND_POLICIES` is gone.\n102-- Reason: two changed docs describe generated tables and a meaning gate; pass one found three doc/code drifts in this area, so the same surface needs a re-read after the fixes.\n103-- Rotation status: correctness and security complete (both PASS); traceability next.\n104-- Blocked/productive carry-forward: security was productive (two P2); no blocked approach.\n105-- Required evidence: the documented numbers against the generated JSON, and the doc's policy-source claim against `advisor-recommend.ts:483`.\n106-\n107-Review verdict: PASS\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"66:- `spec_code` — partial. The `run` policy means \"safe to start without asking\" and the table honours it; the no-edit wording is narrower than the packet's stated intent, recorded as `SA2-P2-002`.\n67-- `checklist_evidence` — pending. No checklist claim in focus.\n68-- `feature_catalog_code` — pending; `command-meaning-matching.md` and the command-bridges README are the traceability iteration's job.\n69-- `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `playbook_capability` — pending / notApplicable.\n70-\n71-## Integration Evidence\n72-\n73-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:478-485` is the only production path that turns an attached command into a `policy`; it reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS` (`:483`), not `COMMAND_ROWS`, which is why the 11 row-less commands still carry a policy.\n74-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:20` imports `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` from the same module, so a widening of the pattern changes the scorer's read-only lift and the attach gate together — the single-vocabulary property the pass-one comment claims.\n75-- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.ts:554-560` keeps the async backend probe on the command path only, so the synchronous recommend reader never performs a network call.\n76-\n77-## Edge Cases\n78-\n79-- **Pattern copied, not widened.** The current `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` is byte-identical to the base `fusion.ts:675` inline regex (`git show 35c3188681:…/fusion.ts`). Recorded so the vocabulary finding is read as pre-existing wording that the new gate now exposes, not as a regression the fix introduced.\n80:- **`start` vs `run`.** Every command the no-edit gap would attach is `start` or `ask`; the only `run` rows are read-only or add-only. That is what keeps `SA2-P2-002` at P2 instead of P1.\n81-- **Row-less commands.** Eleven tracked commands have no `COMMAND_ROWS` entry, so their `mutating` class is not recorded anywhere on the attach path. Read as out of reach for this iteration: those commands are all `start` or `ask`, so the missing class cannot turn into a `run` offer.\n82-\n83-## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n84-\n85-- `command-attach.ts:289` — pattern is a stateless, non-global regex, so repeated `.test()` calls cannot alternate.\n86-- `command-attach.ts:329` — the gate sits before any table lookup and returns `undefined`, so no command and no policy are produced.\n87-- `advisor-status.ts:224-231`, `:318-326` — database handles close on every path, including the error path; a failed close is reported as `unavailable`, not swallowed.\n88-- `advisor-status.ts:424-434` — the integrity probe 