{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597335793,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65621fe0013r0Tv6j2zpWTxF","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d655e946001KkuUx6Oj5loG5y","type":"tool","id":"call_ab0751bec75f420ca67437f3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"hook-wiring-check\\|hook wiring\" .skilled --include=*.md | grep -v node_modules | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_cli-external-orchestration_z_archive_030-cli-cursor-creation_009-cursor-hooks-lifecycle_004-hooks-manual-testing-results_spec.md:121:| Isolated workspace accidentally touches real repo config | Low | Medium (would corrupt live hook wiring) | Explicit git-status check after every dispatch |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_cli-jev_003-cli-jev-workflow-integration_055-alignment-and-hook-parity_spec.md:190:| Risk | 9/25 | Live hook wiring on four runtimes |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-speckit_z_archive_022-hybrid-rag-fusion_007-code-audit-per-feature-catalog_018-ux-hooks_spec.md:73:- Shared post-mutation hook wiring\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-speckit_z_archive_022-hybrid-rag-fusion_007-code-audit-per-feature-catalog_018-ux-hooks_spec.md:221:| F01 | Shared post-mutation hook wiring | MATCH | Implementation matches catalog |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/feature-flag-reference/authored-continuity-snapshot.md:68:Inspect `lib/continuity/authored-continuity-snapshot.ts`, PreCompact hook wiring, and `tests/thin-continuity-record.vitest.ts`. Confirm the sandbox contains the authored ladder files before expecting updates.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/completion-evidence-sentinel.md:354:- Claude hook wiring: `.claude/settings.json` (`hooks.Stop`)\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/session-cleanup-plugin.md:41:mocked stand-ins), and (c) the Claude Code `SessionEnd` hook wiring in `.claude/settings.json`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/session-cleanup-plugin.md:240:- Claude Code hook wiring: `.claude/settings.json` (`SessionEnd` hook)\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/behavior-benchmark/baselines/claude-baseline.md:32:- **Host confound (stated per the framework)**: the baseline runs a different host binary than the opencode legs, so host overhead (session bootstrap, hook wiring) is folded into every latency ratio derived from these values.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/changelog/v3.9.9.0.md:3:description: \"The universal quality floor names each rule with an id, marks it fixed or overridable and keeps only rules that hold in any codebase. Doc-comment forms, typing strictness, naming schemes and this repository's hook wiring leave it.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-hooks/check-dist-staleness-hook.md:103:Catalog: none. `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` does not inventory the shared dist-freshness checker or its hook wiring, so no catalog entry applies to this scenario.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:336:The Catalog Entry column names the feature-catalog document that owns the behavior, as a path relative to `.skilled/skills/sk-code/`. `none` marks a scenario whose behavior the catalog does not inventory: the design-restraint behaviors (DR-001, DR-002, DR-004), the dist-staleness hook wiring (TH-001) and the runtime-neutral post-edit quality router all live in references and hook code the catalog does not list as features, so no catalog entry applies to them.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/hooks.md:3:description: OpenCode-surface reference for current runtime hook wiring, plugin-bridge delivery, dynamic entrypoint reachability, and maintenance rules for editing, adding, or removing hooks.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/hooks.md:16:Reference for the current runtime-hook surfaces in this workspace: checked-in Claude Code hook wiring, checked-in Cursor CLI/editor hook wiring, OpenCode plugin-bridge delivery, and GitHub/Copilot-adjacent hook wrappers. Keep this file aligned with the authoritative hook contract in `system-spec-kit/references/config/hook-system.md` and the live runtime wiring in `.claude/settings.json` / `.cursor/hooks.json`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/hooks.md:44:| Claude settings | `.claude/settings.json` | Live checked-in Claude hook wiring |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/hooks.md:45:| Cursor hooks | `.cursor/hooks.json` | Live checked-in Cursor CLI/editor hook wiring |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/hooks.md:79:Claude Code hook wiring is checked in at `.claude/settings.json`. Use that file as the live wiring source for matchers, command strings, and timeouts.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/hooks.md:116:Cursor CLI hook wiring is checked in at `.cursor/hooks.json` (project scope). Unlike every sibling runtime, this file is **the exact same hooks.json the Cursor desktop editor reads** — project scope merges with (does not shadow) the pre-existing `~/.cursor/hooks.json` user scope, so registering a hook here also applies to any teammate opening this repo in the editor. Use `.cursor/hooks.json` as the live wiring source for matchers, command strings, and timeouts.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/ROUTER.md:36:- **HOOKS** — \"session-prime / user-prompt-submit / pre-tool-use / post-tool-use\" requests load `references/shared/hooks.md` and nothing else, so hook wiring stays in one file.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md:99:| Devin | Hooks inject goal context. The repository exposes no Devin prompt-command surface. | The repository documents hook wiring. A live Devin session is needed to confirm host delivery. ([goal hooks README, lines 75 and 79](../../../../hooks/goal/README.md) and [goal plugin, lines 158 and 162 to 168](../../../../hooks/goal/goal-plugin.md)) |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_cli-external-orchestration_z_archive_030-cli-cursor-creation_009-cursor-hooks-lifecycle_004-hooks-manual-testing-results_spec.md:121:| Isolated workspace accidentally touches real repo config | Low | Medium (would corrupt live hook wiring) | Explicit git-status check after every dispatch |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_cli-jev_003-cli-jev-workflow-integration_055-alignment-and-hook-parity_spec.md:190:| Risk | 9/25 | Live hook wiring on four runtimes |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-speckit_z_archive_022-hybrid-rag-fusion_007-code-audit-per-feature-catalog_018-ux-hooks_spec.md:73:- Shared post-mutation hook wiring\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-speckit_z_archive_022-hybrid-rag-fusion_007-code-audit-per-feature-catalog_018-ux-hooks_spec.md:221:| F01 | Shared post-mutation hook wiring | MATCH | Implementation matches catalog |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/feature-flag-reference/authored-continuity-snapshot.md:68:Inspect `lib/continuity/authored-continuity-snapshot.ts`, PreCompact hook wiring, and `tests/thin-continuity-record.vitest.ts`. Confirm the sandbox contains the authored ladder files before expecting updates.\n.skilled/skills/s