{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794597818617,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"id":"prt_1d65d90f9001fNqrtpXxzuNBs3","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d65d8262001WumVo7gg7fNosH","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597820992,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65d98620014U9TaZFWWqaKVr","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d65d8262001WumVo7gg7fNosH","type":"tool","id":"call_e312d459287a4a1292694517","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '2344,2460p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml"},"output":"      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        instructions: |\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n\n      step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n        action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if active_p0 > 0:\n            release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n          elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n            release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n          else:\n            release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n        outputs:\n          - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n        note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n\n      step_convergence_report:\n        action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n          CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n            --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n            --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n            --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n            --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n            --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n            --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n            --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n            --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n            --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n            --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n          NODE_STATUS=$?\n          for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n            [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n            node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n            GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n            if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n              rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n              exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n            fi\n          done\n          rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n          exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n        note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n\n      step_update_config_status:\n        action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n        set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n\n      step_stage_artifact_dir:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n        command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        instructions: |\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n\n          2. **Planning Trigger**\n             - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n             - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n             - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n             - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n\n          3. **Active Finding Registry**\n             - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n             - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n\n          4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n             - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n\n          5. **Spec Seed**\n             - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n\n          6. **Plan Seed**\n             - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n\n           7. **Traceability Status**\n              - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n              - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n              - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n\n          If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n             - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n             - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n             - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n\n          8. **Deferred Items**\n             - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n\n          **Dimension Expansion Map**\n             - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n             - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n             - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n\n          9. **Search Ledger**\n             - Always include this section before the appendix.\n             - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n             - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n             - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state `hasSearchDebt: true` and carry the dashboard verdict as CONDITIONAL unless active P0 findings make it FAIL.\n\n          10. **Audit Appendix**\n             - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n             - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n\n          Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n        output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n\n      step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n        action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if active_p0 > 0:\n            release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n          elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n            release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n          else:\n            release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n        outputs:\n          - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n        note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n\n      step_convergence_report:\n        action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n          CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n          node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n            --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n            --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n            --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n            --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n            --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n            --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n            --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n            --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n            --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n            --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n          NODE_STATUS=$?\n          for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n            [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n            node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n            GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n            if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n              rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n              exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n            fi\n          done\n          rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n          exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n        note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n\n      step_update_config_status:\n        action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n        set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n\n      step_stage_artifact_dir:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n        command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '2344,2460p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597820514,"end":1794597820992}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597820997,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65d941f0016EB2g7cQdotSGo","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d65d8262001WumVo7gg7fNosH","type":"tool","id":"call_bcbf0e9b9d9f4989a36a97af","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"no-edit\\|NO_EDIT\\|no change\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md | head -10; echo \"=== lib README ===\"; sed -n '128,136p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md; echo \"=== scorer README 50-58 ===\"; sed -n '50,58p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md"},"output":"36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n=== lib README ===\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n| `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. The module has no imports. |\n| `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n| `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n| `skill-advisor-brief.ts` | Builds concise advisor recommendation briefs. |\n| `normalize-adapter-output.ts` | Normalizes adapter result shapes. |\n=== scorer README 50-58 ===\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `fusion.ts` | Combines lane scores into final advisor ranking signals through RRF fusion, with a conflict-match rerank seam and a self-recommendation guard that penalizes advisor self-recommendations. `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` keeps a passing command row passing only when the explicit-author lane matched one of its own phrases or its slash string, or when it passes on meaning: a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72) with a lead of `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02) over the next command row. The word-overlap stand-in used under test never counts. `commandMeaningEligible` decides who may pass on meaning: a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the pattern `readOnlyRouteAllowed` also reads, rules out every command, and a read-only explainer admits only a command whose route only reads. `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves a meaning-passed command ahead of the top passing skill only when its cosine leads that skill's by the same margin. |\n| `lane-registry.ts` | Registers available scoring lanes. |\n| `aliases.ts` | Canonicalizes explicit command/skill alias groups for route comparisons. |\n| `attribution.ts` | Builds prompt-safe lane attribution details. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n=== lib README ===\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n| `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. The module has no imports. |\n| `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n| `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n| `skill-advisor-brief.ts` | Builds concise advisor recommendation briefs. |\n| `normalize-adapter-output.ts` | Normalizes adapter result shapes. |\n=== scorer README 50-58 ===\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `fusion.ts` | Combines lane scores into final advisor ranking signals through RRF fusion, with a conflict-match rerank seam and a self-recommendation guard that penalizes advisor self-recommendations. `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` keeps a passing command row passing only when the explicit-author lane matched one of its own phrases or its slash string, or when it passes on meaning: a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72) with a lead of `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02) over the next command row. The word-overlap stand-in used under test never counts. `commandMeaningEligible` decides who may pass on meaning: a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the pattern `readOnlyRouteAllowed` also reads, rules out every command, and a read-only explainer admits only a command whose route only reads. `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves a meaning-passed command ahead of the top passing skill only when its cosine leads that skill's by the same margin. |\n| `lane-registry.ts` | Registers available scoring lanes. |\n| `aliases.ts` | Canonicalizes explicit command/skill alias groups for route comparisons. |\n| `attribution.ts` | Builds prompt-safe lane attribution details. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"no-edit\\\\|NO_EDIT\\\\|no change\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md | head -10; echo \\\"=== lib README ===\\\"; sed -n '128,136p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md; echo \\\"=== scorer README 50-58 ===\\\"; sed -n '50,58p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597819423,"end":1794597820997}}}}
