{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794597857138,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"id":"prt_1d65e2772001HivUEv0Hdcdyco","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d65e1c7c0012hNT3AveYO6C8R","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597870935,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65e57f0001Gb2i6odYAwkg7G","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d65e1c7c0012hNT3AveYO6C8R","type":"tool","id":"call_8161c4ad4a634217a88b0c01","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && S=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && ls \"$S\" | head -20; echo \"=== checklist ===\"; ls \"$S\"/checklist.md 2>/dev/null || echo \"no checklist.md\"; echo \"=== spec mentions ===\"; grep -rn \"NO_EDIT\\|no-edit\\|hook-wiring\" \"$S\" --include=*.md | grep -v \"review/\" | head -10; echo \"=== advisor playbook ===\"; ls -d .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook 2>/dev/null || echo \"no advisor playbook dir\""},"output":"001-command-routing-baseline-corpus\n002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata\n003-plain-chat-command-reach\n004-command-meaning-matching\n005-recommendation-contract-and-brief\n006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost\n009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research\n010-reachability-and-attribution\n011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n012-plain-offer-reach\n013-attribution-and-install-reach\n014-review-remediation\n015-health-default-and-brief-refinements\n016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n017-review-pass-two-remediation\n018-holdout-row-retirement\ndecision-record.md\ndescription.json\n=== checklist ===\nno checklist.md\n=== spec mentions ===\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:50:A fault in the middle of an embed now ends in a verified restore or a printed reason why not, and it exits 3. The hub attach path no longer offers a writing command on a no-edit prompt, a file name or a mention of another deep-loop command. The renderer tests pass inside a dispatched child. A live behaviour arm now runs only in a marked arena with an allowlisted environment.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:56:`command-attach.ts` now owns `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, and `fusion.ts` imports it. The deep-loop gate opens only for the command being attached or for depth wording. A dot or a slash followed by a word character continues a file name, so `/create:skill.md` is no typed command. The deriver no longer emits `COMMAND_POLICIES`, and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` is the one attach-path table.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:72:| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modified, Created | The shared no-edit pattern, the deep-loop gate, the file-name boundary and the absent policy table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:73:| `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Modified | Imports `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and drops an empty branch |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:78:| `DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and their two tests | Modified | Flag-value refusal, the absent-entry repair line and the wiring matcher |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:112:| The shared `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` pattern stays as it is. This was decided without the operator, under goal decision D1, with no code change | A prompt that only limits the scope of a change, such as \"create a skill and do not change the existing skills\", keeps its skill and loses the command. That fails toward no offer and matches what the scorer path already did |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:115:| Wave 4 (T062 to T073) was added after the first verifier reports | It fixes what they flagged. That covers a stderr cap test that passed without the fix, the bench header, the hook-wiring matcher, the unguarded restore, a detached comment, the symlink status precedence, the symlink-blind entry guard, an arena comment, the Pi header read order, the raw id on a needs-a-mode head, the holdout empty-set guard and three README sentences |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:135:| T058 probes | `main returned 3`, `restored line: true`, `after: CLAUDE.md`, `plan exit=2` with `ci.yml` digests `b8ae3686e91b` before and after, `undefined` on the no-edit, `/deep:ai-council` and file-name lines, `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in module -> false`, `(needs a mode)` and `(parent-named only)` on the two render lines and 15 `apply exit 0` lines |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:158:1. **The hook-wiring matcher misreads some shell shapes.** It reads `true; node <script>` and `cd x;node <script>` as missing and `echo 'x && node <script>'` as wired. It also reads `node --no-warnings <script>`, `/usr/bin/env node <script>` and `zsh -c 'node <script>'` as missing. No Skilled installer writes any of these shapes, so this is recorded and not built.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:161:4. **A third copy of the no-edit wording remains.** `scorer/text.ts` line 148 keeps its own pattern. The plan records it, and this phase may not edit that file.\n=== advisor playbook ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0}