{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597917036,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65f0d990015NsvuPhVEI7JQx","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d95affeG1NNpWx5iqRIiD","messageID":"msg_1d65eddd3001oIDxbwhM9tPlOe","type":"tool","id":"call_6d5413c5237d425f9e5c3419","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"no-edit\\|NO_EDIT\\|make no changes\\|hook-wiring\\|hook wiring\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -12"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:56:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given an agent request ending in each of the four no-edit wordings, When the attach path, the scorer gate and the explainer test read it, Then no command attaches, the gate says `false` and a read-only request reads as read-only | `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` report 0 failed with the T003 to T005 cases, and `probe-no-edit.mts` prints `undefined` on its five attach lines and `false` on its five scorer lines. Observed: `VALL` reads `Tests 1796 passed` with 0 failed at `scratch/after.txt:19`, which includes the three files, and the five attach lines and five scorer lines end at `scratch/repro-after.txt:96` and `scratch/repro-after.txt:101` with `-> undefined` and `-> false` on each | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:82:| AC-027 | REQ-027 | Given the seven wrapper launches and a quoted `echo` of the script, When the hook-wiring check reads them, Then the launches read `ok` and the `echo` reads `hook-missing` | The T034 cases pass in `NT $HWT`, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok` for claude, codex, cursor and devin, and `probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints the T034 lines. Observed in close-out reruns: `NT $HWT` reads `pass 28` and `fail 0`, and `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and exits 0. `scratch/repro-after.txt:73` prints `bash -lc: exit 0 ok claude`, the nine launch lines all read `exit 0 ok claude`, and `scratch/repro-after.txt:79` prints `echo with a quoted script: exit 1 hook-missing` | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:35:      - \"The widened no-edit pattern moved no holdout aggregate: EVAL reads [160,50,21,5] before and after\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:66:- **WG1, the shared no-edit gate.** `command-attach.ts` exports `isNoEditRequest`, which folds curly apostrophes to straight ones and tests the widened `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`. `attachCommand`, both scorer gates in `fusion.ts` and `isReadOnlyExplainer` in `text.ts` call it, so `text.ts` holds no copy of the wording now. The status privacy case stores a record and checks status hides it. The attach test lost its assertion that never reached a gate. The command-bridges README names all four `CommandRow` fields, held by a test. `tsString` escapes LF, CR, U+2028 and U+2029 and is exported for its new round-trip test.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:74:- **WG9, doctor checks.** `hook-wiring-check.cjs` splits a command into simple commands outside quotes and reads `env`, `bash`, `sh` and `zsh` wrappers. A10 counts only `PASS` copies as expected and names report-only copies apart.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:95:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `agents-md-check.cjs`, `tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` | Modified | Quote-aware launch reader, A10 count (WG9) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:112:| T003 and REQ-001 widen `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` with a bare `no changes` | The pattern holds `make no changes\\|no changes yet` (T042), and `rg -c \"make no changes\\|no changes yet\"` on `command-attach.ts` prints 1 | Verifier finding F1 showed the bare form read \"refactor the parser so there are no changes to its public api\" as a no-edit request. `spec.md` REQ-001 was reworded to the narrowed form after the close-out |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:133:| Narrow the no-edit pattern to `make no changes\\|no changes yet` (T042) | The bare form took the command from change requests that limit their scope. Three such requests now read `false` in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, and every floor held |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:176:7. **The `sh` shell has no hook-wiring case of its own.** `bash` and `zsh` have cases, and the reader checks all three names from one list.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:178:9. **`spec.md` REQ-001 was reworded after the close-out.** It now names `make no changes` and `no changes yet` and says why the bare form was dropped.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/plan.md:57:- **`isNoEditRequest` in `command-attach.ts`**: the one place a prompt is normalised and 